In the early game before mcuh spell casting makes sense, the
thrown dagger is the wizard's primary weapon.  By the end game
that dagger equals a (Q)uiver of a dozen or so highly enchanted
fireproof elven daggers.  So avoid melee by barrage after barrage
of thrown daggers.

Did you deliberately avoid altars?  If you didn't it's clear you
didn't #offer enough.  Magicbane is the first gift to a wizard and
the chances are only 1-in-25 or better once reconciled.

But one lesson of Nethack is multilayered defense and offense.
Just because a wizard uses daggers and/or spells as his/her
primary offense doesn't mean melee gets ignored.  Do enough
melee with popcorn monsters to be able to increase your skill
to basic in broadsword (Stormy) or long sword (Vorpy, banes)
and get one good artifact highly enchanted.

Even with a blessed +5 silver saber, an archon softened up
by a dozen thrown daggers will only need a couple of whacks
in melee to die.

